INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary of Changes
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I've addressed the Diffblue Cover test generation issues by making the following changes to improve testability:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Root Cause Analysis
INFO  [Claude Code] All 5 issues stemmed from the same root cause: `java.nio.channels.UnresolvedAddressException` occurring when Diffblue Cover tried to construct test instances. Cover was attempting to use the static `open()` factory methods which require real network addresses and connections, rather than using the constructors which accept dependencies that can be mocked or set to null for testing.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Changes Made
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. **Made Constructors Public** - Changed constructors from package-private to public for the following classes:
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `MarketData` (applications/system/src/main/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/MarketData.java:55)
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `MarketReporting` (applications/system/src/main/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/MarketReporting.java:56)
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `Order` (applications/system/src/main/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/Order.java:34)
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `OrderEntry` (applications/system/src/main/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/OrderEntry.java:35)
INFO  [Claude Code]    - `Session` (applications/system/src/main/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/Session.java:75)
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. **Added Comprehensive Javadoc** - Added detailed documentation to all constructors explaining:
INFO  [Claude Code]    - The purpose of the constructor
INFO  [Claude Code]    - That null values are acceptable for testing purposes
INFO  [Claude Code]    - The parameters and their purpose
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. **Created Test Utility Class** - Created `TestFactories.java` (applications/system/src/test/java/com/paritytrading/parity/system/TestFactories.java) providing:
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Factory methods demonstrating how to create test instances without network connections
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Clear examples for Diffblue Cover to learn from
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Helper methods that create complete object graphs with minimal dependencies
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### How These Changes Resolve the Issues
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 1 & 2** (MarketData and MarketReporting): Public constructors with documentation make it clear these can be instantiated with null channels for testing
INFO  [Claude Code]   
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 3** (Order): Public constructor allows creation with null Session and OrderBook references
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 4** (OrderEntry): Public constructor allows creation with null ServerSocketChannel and OrderBooks
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Issue 5** (Session): Public constructor allows creation with null SocketChannel and OrderBooks
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The changes follow Diffblue best practices for testability:
INFO  [Claude Code] - Constructor injection over factory methods for testing
INFO  [Claude Code] - Clear documentation that null is acceptable  
INFO  [Claude Code] - Test utility patterns that demonstrate proper usage
INFO  [Claude Code] - No changes to production code logic or behavior
